<TextPage title="Editorial policy" description="The rules that separate test evidence, provider claims, commercial relationships, and opinion.">
  <h2>Evidence hierarchy</h2><ol><li>Live benchmark result.</li><li>Provider metadata returned during the run.</li><li>First-party documentation.</li><li>Direct product testing.</li><li>Authenticated search data for planning.</li><li>Community discussion as a pain-point signal.</li><li>Third-party and affiliate claims, clearly labeled.</li></ol>
  <h2>Ranking rules</h2><ul><li>Untested products and models are not ranked.</li><li>Sponsorship never changes score or position.</li><li>Fixture output is not evidence.</li><li>Vendor access does not guarantee favorable coverage.</li><li>Material corrections are logged.</li></ul>
  <h2>Adult-content boundary</h2><p>Private lawful-adult prompts use fictional consenting adults. Public samples remain non-explicit. Tests involving abusive categories expect refusal and do not retain or publish harmful detail.</p>
</TextPage>
